<h1 dir="auto" class="text-3xl">Outline: <em>From Catharsis to Geometric Bayesian Emotion: RSVP and the Demise of the Hydraulic Model</em></h1>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><strong class="font-semibold">Abstract</strong>
We critique the catharsis model of emotionâ€”derived from Freudian hydraulics and still culturally pervasiveâ€”as theoretically incoherent. Rather than â€œreleasingâ€ pressure, indulging sadness or anger re-excites the same dynamical attractors, prolonging emotional dwell time. We propose a replacement grounded in Relativistic Scalar Vector Plenum (RSVP) field dynamics and Geometric Bayesianism with Sparse Heuristics (GBSH). Emotions are attractor basins in constrained inference geometry, shaped by metabolic sparsity and comparative reference frames. This framework explains why catharsis amplifies affect, why reframing alters valence without arousal escalation, and why personality â€œtraitsâ€ are environmental averages rather than fixed quantities.</p>
