</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(2980.8px);"><span><span>The RSVPâ€“GBSH model has far-reaching applications in clinical psychology, AI design, and education. In therapy, rejecting catharsis favors cognitive reframing techniques, such as shifting reference priors to alter valence without escalating arousalâ€”supported by evidence from CBT and mindfulness interventions. Phenotype-aware projections (e.g., low </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\(</span><span>g</span><span style="color: rgb(230, 192, 123);">_</span><span>I</span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\)</span><span>) suggest personalized approaches for alexithymia or aphantasia, where external tools compensate for absent qualia.
</span></span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3002.4px);"><span>
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3024px);"><span>In AI, sparse heuristics inform efficient architectures: metabolic analogs (energy budgets) yield robust, biomimetic agents that avoid exhaustive search. Educational implications include teaching comparative thinking to mitigate emotional loops, fostering resilience through attractor reshaping.
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3045.6px);"><span>
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3067.2px);"><span>Cross-culturally, the framework predicts varied emotional ecologies: classifier-rich languages correlate with graded affect, while binary-dominant cultures emphasize dichotomous reasoning. Future research could integrate physiological data (HRV, EDA) with field simulations for real-time interventions.
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3088.8px);"><span>
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3110.4px);"><span>Ethically, this shifts focus from "venting" to structural change, reducing risks of amplification in vulnerable populations.
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3132px);"><span>
