</span></span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3175.2px);"><span>
</span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3196.8px);"><span>Catharsis remains an incoherent relic of hydraulic models, perpetuating feedback that it claims to resolve. RSVPâ€“GBSH offers a unified alternative, framing emotions as emergent attractors in sparse, geometric Bayesian fields. Escape requires reframing structures, not expression. Path forward: rigorous experiments on reframing, constraints, and oscillations, bridging theory to practice.
