</span></span></div><div style="position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 100%; height: 1.5em; transform: translateY(3801.6px);"><span><span>Languages start with many categories, like sorting objects by shape or use. Over time, social pressures simplify these into a few, then just two (e.g., male/female), reinforced by stories like Noahâ€™s Ark. This binary thinking becomes the foundation for true/false logic </span><span style="color: rgb(198, 120, 221);">\citep</span><span>{Kneale1962}.
